# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This matters for dsh-cookie-rescue.sh: a CRLF shebang line makes bash fail
# with "bad interpreter" on Linux and macOS, and the failure looks like a
# broken script rather than a checkout problem. Pinning LF removes that risk
# entirely, regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch/PowerShell files are conventionally CRLF, but .ps1 runs fine
# with LF and keeping one rule everywhere avoids surprise diffs.
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Never let Git touch binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
